  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "yajYmWUIihbgOOfEjH0JVhFZ6q0=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:54:28.835Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The Todo List is the worked example used throughout the Build track, and the reference implementation at **`powerhouse-inc/todo-tutorial`** is organised so a learner never has to start from scratch:\n\n- each step has a **starting branch** (`step-1-\u2026`) and a **completed branch** (`step-1-complete-\u2026`);\n- the `step-1-` branch **matches what `ph init todo-tutorial` produces**, so a local project and the repository begin identical;\n- comparing work against a checkpoint is `git diff your-branch step-1-complete-\u2026`, or \"compare with branch\" in the GitHub UI.\n\nOne setup detail is easy to get wrong and expensive: when forking, **uncheck \"copy the main branch only\"** \u2014 otherwise every step branch is lost and the diff workflow the tutorial is built on stops working. Then clone the fork and `pnpm install`.\n\nWhat the finished package demonstrates, which doubles as a map of the Build track: a `TodoList` document model with state schema and operations; reducer operation handlers **and their unit tests**; a document editor wired to the model's operations; a custom **Drive Explorer** for managing many Todo Lists in a drive; and a shared component displaying stats in **both** the editor and the Drive Explorer \u2014 the last one being the piece that shows a component crossing the editor/drive-app boundary.\n\nThe same example is taught twice on purpose: the Manual Todo tutorial builds a basic package by hand, and the Document Model Creation mastery track re-derives it with the theory plus advanced extensions (computed `stats`, the Drive Explorer, the shared component).\n\n## Provenance\n- `apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/06-ExampleUsecases/TodoList/TodoList.md` \u2014 whole page: the reference repository, branch conventions, what the finished package demonstrates\n- `apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/01-ManualTodoTutorial/01-CreateNewPowerhouseProject.md` \u2014 Setup: create your project and connect to tutorial repo; Compare your work with reference steps\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:54:28.835Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:54:28.835Z"
    }
  },
